From f2fefb75866a7e12c30ab0819e06b856a16c00b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 16/21] pci: symmetric bring-up and teardown, with runtime
 power management

Factor the hardware bring-up and teardown into fthd_pm_up() and
fthd_pm_down() and use them for probe, remove, shutdown and both kinds
of suspend. With facetimehd.runtime_pm=1, an open file holds a
runtime-PM reference and the camera powers down after the last close;
the default leaves the device powered.

Reference-count the private data so an open file outlives PCI unbind
and fails with -ENODEV; disconnect V4L2 before releasing hardware;
serialise V4L2 with ioctl_lock; map BARs with pci_iomap(); handle AER
by marking the device wedged; and unwind partial ISP initialisation.
System suspend no longer refuses an open device: it stops the stream
and errors the queue.
